  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "Dividend Policy In March 2018, the Board\nof Directors suspended the payment of dividends on our Common Stock. The Board of Directors also suspended the quarterly dividends on\nshares of our Series A Preferred Stock, Series B Preferred Stock and Series D Preferred Stock, beginning with the three months ended\nDecember 31, 2018. Dividends were suspended to retain cash flow to pay operating expenses and reduce debt. On November 3, 2021, common\nstockholders of the Company voted to amend the Charter to remove the cumulative dividend rights of the Series A Preferred Stock and Series\nB Preferred Stock. Additionally, as the Company has failed to pay cash dividends on the outstanding Series D Preferred Stock, the annual\ndividend rate on the Series D Preferred Stock increased to 10.75% commencing on the first day after the first missed quarterly payment,\nJanuary 1, 2019, and will continue increasing",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
